/** @page mongodbreleasehistory mongodb Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section mongodb_3_0 mongodb Module Version 3.0
    - initial release
    - BSON array construction uses the supported libbson 2.3 API while retaining
      compatibility with older drivers; array keys remain contiguous from zero,
      including null elements and nested arrays
    - array conversion honors thread cancellation and sandbox interruption,
      including large arrays, while preserving cleanup deferral
    - a call blocked on the server (connecting, the TLS handshake, reading or writing) ends as soon as the thread
      is cancelled or its Program is interrupted, instead of within 500 ms: connections use a socket of the
      module's own whose waits are woken directly by the request
